Provenance / third-party attribution

The decoding algorithm and numeric tables in src/tinymp2_tables.h and
src/tinymp2_decoder.h were ported from the MPEG-1 Layer II ("MP2") audio
decoder in PL_MPEG:

  PL_MPEG - MPEG1 Video decoder, MP2 Audio decoder, MPEG-PS demuxer
  Copyright (c) Dominic Szablewski - https://phoboslab.org
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
  https://github.com/phoboslab/pl_mpeg

which in turn credits its MP2 audio decoder as based on kjmp2 by Martin J.
Fiedler (http://keyj.emphy.de/kjmp2/), released under permissive terms by its
author.

TinyMP2 is an independent reimplementation for header-only, allocation-free
microcontroller use: the file layout, the BitReader, the C++ class structure,
and the streaming/Arduino-facing API are original to this project, but the
core numerics (bit-allocation quantizer tables, the 512-tap synthesis window,
the dequantization formula, and the polyphase synthesis filter) are the same
as PL_MPEG's, and have been cross-validated bit-for-bit against it.
